  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-000",
      "source": "sections/sec-000-acknowledgements.md",
      "source_hash": "0274388c80879e3e78cb642882411d48b745a6fffce13196fa02a9e9f997b6cd",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Acknowledges the authors, WHO contributors, reviewers and Gavi funding for the district and facility analysis guidance, followed by a list of abbreviations. The abbreviations range across health services, programmes and information systems, such as ANC, ART, RHIS and UHC.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-guidance-overview.md",
      "source_hash": "47ad34b26c3665286c30044a937e8ddedc4e9a00ef4fd2311ad815e675576e60",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Places the document within WHO's Toolkit for analysis and use of routine health facility data, which promotes standardized core indicators, analyses and dashboards across programmes. It describes the toolkit's components and explains that this guidance offers district and facility managers examples of using routine data for decisions, without covering district management in full.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-learning-objectives.md",
      "source_hash": "ae1e3fba77684fe8b2a324602a91fc9f41e90942bb79a54d9d0328b19f3ce8b2",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States the learning objectives of the guidance: a focused set of indicators in three groups, standard visualizations in integrated dashboards and their use in meetings and supervision. It defines the target audience of district managers and analysts and lists suggested reading.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-11-district-health-system.md",
      "source_hash": "37f8b970a67e1db4c9c8100dc0b5e484083ec2051a55ad952abf3d21af2ea99a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the district health system as a network of primary care facilities under a district hospital and management team, possibly including private providers, and explains how the term is used in the guidance.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-12-data-needs-of-district-and-facility-managers.md",
      "source_hash": "9f4671b598dc3a7e4f43963b38ad69f6304a9716de06744b3c7b2a35e01a4fbe",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists the responsibilities of district and facility managers, such as meeting policies, responding to events, ensuring access and using resources efficiently, and their need for routine data and context to fulfil them.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-13-data-sources-at-subnational-level.md",
      "source_hash": "62c0e8b9235e58e9f263f3743d15ac661b2d07c36ce3fa98b80e1388ee296921",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that the guidance focuses on aggregate routine health information system data while noting other sources within the broader health information system, such as surveys, censuses and surveillance.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-131-routine-health-information-system-rhis.md",
      "source_hash": "477d889b42f694a955755213131561c4b0abec48d7dab0bb617c806155ad01cf",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the routine data that health facilities collect and report on diseases, service outputs and outcomes, and how often they are reported. It also outlines related information systems, including surveillance, human resources, logistics and financial management systems.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-134-population-data.md",
      "source_hash": "3906636df53d7545d565943737690ec49ff8263fa087d157a3f04a5b63260e28",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses the difficulty of obtaining reliable population denominators, especially for facility catchment areas, and recommends analyses that avoid them, such as trends in absolute numbers and facility-based denominators. It also notes other information sources that help interpret district data.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-14-principles-of-this-guidance.md",
      "source_hash": "e2147bdc17bfe4f1476fdd8d4e88af3907bd5ee9e7904c7e30519d8544293d51",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces the five principles behind the guidance, building on the toolkit's general principles and national-level documents.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-142-focused-analysis---using-a-limited-set-of-in.md",
      "source_hash": "e12de2396579ef9bdd8d28089bdaf9a506edd30bbde55fee56ae852e3f1b2296",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains the principles of integration across programmes and of focusing on a limited set of tracer indicators to flag problems. It also discusses keeping disaggregation manageable to protect data quality, noting that WHO does not recommend sex disaggregation of routine childhood immunization data.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-143-standardization---of-indicators-analyses-and.md",
      "source_hash": "2bdd8a47159d1b2af213d23e8da2fc8f5509a5800d5adee6862afb2e0a4c2c8c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes standardizing indicators, analyses and visualizations so data can be compared, and introduces sample dashboards for facility and district levels over monthly and annual timeframes. It warns against cluttered electronic dashboards and stresses assessing and acknowledging data quality alongside analysis.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "source": "sections/sec-012-145-purpose-oriented-analysis---for-management-a.md",
      "source_hash": "12aafad7f60224725d6d1bd38ccff507467bcc3a46eac9a6f17617d4dad3f28a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that routine data should inform short-term decisions from recent months and longer-term planning from yearly trends, with a framework table linking analysis types to management actions such as redeploying resources or adjusting supervision.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-151-ways-to-analyse-rhis-data.md",
      "source_hash": "ed9d128ffb4cd2fca077b5bbc1e1da174d52d62c9ed09da7ba0cf500bd148f1f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains how to clean routine data and analyse it through comparisons over time, between diseases, among facilities and against populations or targets. It describes suitable charts and tables for answering questions of when, who, what and where, with guidance on interpreting trends and outliers. A country example from Sierra Leone shows how simple tracking of immunization at facility level improved measles coverage.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-152-interpretation-and-communication-of-rhis-dat.md",
      "source_hash": "428adffc772944b4e55b10137ad4fbf0acceec03ec42703f09383243a367bf43",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes how regular district review meetings and the distribution of printed dashboards can involve a wide range of staff in interpreting routine data. It covers meeting participants, preparation and follow-up, and ways of sending dashboards to facilities and managers as feedback.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-161-lupara-district-database.md",
      "source_hash": "b7c2a1aa5dd8a59bebca9b23b244ce12d12eec20fa571520da4b33ffc08ecf9b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces the fictitious \"Lupara\" district Excel database used to demonstrate the sample dashboards, explaining that its data are adapted and do not represent any real place or good data quality. It describes the dashboard naming scheme by level, timeframe and indicator group. The section ends with review questions asking readers to compare different dashboards.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
