        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-032",
      "source": "sections/sec-032-313-core-analysis.md",
      "source_hash": "b73ef323a8b59ff888a175d7e3fb93239a633741629b04e993024d4714075035",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents core analyses of service utilization, starting with outpatient visits per capita, for which no benchmark exists but trends should be monitored, illustrated with five years of Lupara district data. Further indicators include emergency unit use, inpatient utilization, surgical volume and service-specific availability. A map shows the hospitals providing caesarean sections, with dot size proportional to the number performed in 2019.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-034",
      "source": "sections/sec-034-321-service-output-and-coverage-indicators.md",
      "source_hash": "5e51ddcd2c61bbfd8ef8e736864ba97916d88680b0659df3dc5e6ccb02fbf748",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A table of service output and coverage indicators, such as antenatal visits, facility deliveries, immunization coverage and new diabetes cases, giving definitions, calculations, disaggregation and reporting level.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-035",
      "source": "sections/sec-035-322-about-the-data.md",
      "source_hash": "764c0ffa87cad84700acc2fe84f261633c31cfe9ee74f69806ec88883ca01ed0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines service coverage and service outputs and explains that reported outputs can serve as proxies for coverage where reliable population denominators are lacking. It distinguishes coverage from quality indicators and explains why PMTCT testing is classed as a quality measure in this guidance.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-036",
      "source": "sections/sec-036-323-core-analysis.md",
      "source_hash": "9401cbad0597e32c484f2006e04e228799776e5fa5124f032d8be12589e02500",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes a sample set of tracer coverage indicators, beginning with antenatal visits in line with WHO's recommendation of eight contacts starting in the first trimester. Other tracers include institutional deliveries, immunization and the detection of conditions such as hypertension and diabetes. Questions direct readers to interpret trends on the sample Lupara facility dashboards.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-038",
      "source": "sections/sec-038-331-quality-indicators.md",
      "source_hash": "ff13deab454551b30d532ab915ddb8de1e022228dbae7a6b4e9be873bd55445c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A table of health service quality indicators, such as early antenatal visits, PMTCT testing, malaria prevention in pregnancy, immunization dropout and inpatient outcomes, with their definitions and calculations. It notes that readmissions can signal inadequate care and that adequate resources are a prerequisite for quality services.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-039",
      "source": "sections/sec-039-332-about-the-data.md",
      "source_hash": "8a506ba951ec640b9eacdfeeb2de20678bc397443c82c326c337fbaba95688ff",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines health service quality as delivery according to required standards and explains its importance for universal health coverage, noting that quality has many dimensions. It states that the section covers process and outcome indicators, with resource indicators left to the next chapter.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-369381/blocks/prose-sec-040",
      "source": "sections/sec-040-333-core-analysis.md",
      "source_hash": "acdf6b3597caab57a01128458af9dcee7dec0859135f22e07cf3a66722ff6b96",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Works through core quality indicators, explaining what each reveals, such as early antenatal care, PMTCT testing and malaria preventive treatment in pregnancy. Others include caesarean section rates, immunization dropout and the HIV care cascade, plus inpatient and malaria case management measures. A Lupara district table of values ends with a question asking readers to spot suspicious findings, such as treatment percentages above 100%.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
